{"id": "EUVD-2026-86658", "enisaUuid": "b53459cf-9474-302a-b3f6-1c69a8397690", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nerofs: delimit inode_share cache key components\n\nPreviously, inode_share keys were encoded as follows:\n\n  fingerprint || domain_id\n\nIt would be better to have a separator between the fingerprint and domain\nID so that the fingerprint won't be parsed as part of a domain ID.\n\nChange the key encoding as follows:\n\n  domain_id || '\\0' || fingerprint\n\nSince domain_id is a NUL-terminated string, this makes the in-memory key\nindices unambiguous.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:12:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16322a67336cfeea0af4b05206ef8d0e0eda55bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/96bf9831fbf423b8104f7948cd8fe7007ecfb46c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cmc8-g72c-8f33", "CVE-2026-98005"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "279add89-ca76-35eb-b072-e348280ee1f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "41998f1f-d92b-3d13-9a1b-9f51ac23cc77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "84583da7-8074-3cbf-b3f6-00bd26d364d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e0bf7d1c074dc4252223ae897560345ccc24100d <96bf9831fbf423b8104f7948cd8fe7007ecfb46c"}, {"id": "8c36fbed-d452-3331-95e9-9c3fef91db17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "ab2b11a3-ad32-3909-8de9-580a98aa3316", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0"}, {"id": "b6e55b40-ff9f-3b5b-b3fc-d2f165093437", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e0bf7d1c074dc4252223ae897560345ccc24100d <16322a67336cfeea0af4b05206ef8d0e0eda55bb"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "